sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch02-16> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Practical computing shows that it is usually very difficult to foresee the behavior of even a simple program, which is why software bugs are so common; the simple structure of cellular automaton rules likewise does not make their behavior easy to predict.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "It is usually very hard to foresee what even a simple program will do";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 2, “The Crucial Experiment”; section “Why These Discoveries Were Not Made Before” (from p. 42), p. 46. Scope: simple programs, including software and cellular automata"
}
